# ML and Causal Rules

1. Anomaly detection goes through a quantitative detector when one is available.
2. Forecasting uses only models registered in `config/model_registry.yaml` (targets are catalogue `metric.*` ids) or approved statistical baselines.
3. Every model output carries model version, applicability, validation/backtest and drift metadata.
4. DoWhy requests must specify treatment, outcome, causal graph and confounder assumptions.
5. Run causal refutation/sensitivity checks required by the causal registry.
6. LLMs may propose derived features but cannot promote them directly into production.
7. Detect and prevent temporal leakage in all predictive features.
